{
  "schema_version": "locator_index_v1",
  "source_id": "MAC-010",
  "source_sha256": "8fac4146590dbe2ed458f7356748f5880d021e03cc4982b1e7efe083d33f622a",
  "locator": "page 60",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "S00001",
      "start_char": 0,
      "end_char": 204,
      "text": "MEXICO\nAnnex III. Debt Sustainability Analysis\nA. Sovereign Risk and Debt Sustainability Analysis\nAnnex III. Figure 1. Mexico: Risk of Sovereign Stress\nMechanical Final\nHorizon Comments\nsignal assessment\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00002",
      "start_char": 204,
      "end_char": 427,
      "text": "The overall risk of sovereign stress is judged to be moderate. The\nOverall … Moderate post-pandemic recovery is expected to slow slightly in 2023 as global\nconditions deteriorate, resulting in elevated debt levels and non-\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00003",
      "start_char": 427,
      "end_char": 628,
      "text": "stabilization of debt by 2027. However, a return to trend growth and\na tight fiscal stance will help contain the debt path and more\nfavorable conditions will see debt decline over the extended 10-year\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00004",
      "start_char": 628,
      "end_char": 817,
      "text": "period. While the balanced budget rule in the fiscal framework plays\na role in containing debt, the impact on budget composition could\nbe a long-run issue as expenditures on investment and\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00005",
      "start_char": 817,
      "end_char": 1003,
      "text": "deveopmental objectives are often restrained to ensure compliance\nwith the rule.\nNear term 1/\nMedium term Moderate Moderate Medium-term risks are assessed as moderate. Fanchart analysis\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00006",
      "start_char": 1003,
      "end_char": 1239,
      "text": "suggests that baseline projections are reasonable but risks remain\nFanchart Moderate …\naround the non-stabilization of debt by the end of the projection\nGFN Moderate … period. GFN analysis indicates that financing needs will be broadly\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00007",
      "start_char": 1239,
      "end_char": 1454,
      "text": "stable. The standardized stress tests suggest that additional\nStress test ... … financing needs could reach close to 15 percent in a stress scenario\nbut the domestic banking and non-depository sectors could pick up\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00008",
      "start_char": 1454,
      "end_char": 1653,
      "text": "slack. The balanced budget rule assists in containing debt but may\nhave implications for budget composition.\nThe persistence of medium-term factors may serve to affect the long-\nLong term … Moderate\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00009",
      "start_char": 1653,
      "end_char": 1871,
      "text": "run outlook. The impact of a restrictive fiscal stance and the absence\nof structural reforms may pose a trade-off between long-run growth\nand budget balance, meaning that debt ratios may not achieve a\ndeclining trend.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00010",
      "start_char": 1871,
      "end_char": 2095,
      "text": "The projected debt path and GFN are expected to increase\nsomewhat over the main projection period but decline over the\nSustainable\nSustainability extended 10-year period. Debt is therefore judged to be sustainable\nwith high\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00011",
      "start_char": 2095,
      "end_char": 2313,
      "text": "assessment 2/ but notable risks from further shocks remain, particularly given the\nprobability\nglobal macroeconomic context and the tight fiscal stance\nunderpinning debt dynamics.\nDebt stabilization in the baseline No\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00012",
      "start_char": 2313,
      "end_char": 2446,
      "text": "DSA Summary Assessment\nStaff Commentary: The risk of Mexico experiencing sovereign stress is moderate overall and its public debt is\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00013",
      "start_char": 2446,
      "end_char": 2666,
      "text": "assessed to be sustainable with high probability over the extended time horizon. While still manageable under\nmost downside scenarios, fan chart analysis suggests that public debt ratios could increase materially in the\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00014",
      "start_char": 2666,
      "end_char": 2838,
      "text": "medium-term, possibly constraining policy options and leading to moderate risks of sovereign stress compared\nto low risks in the near term.\nSource: IMF staff calculations.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00015",
      "start_char": 2838,
      "end_char": 3060,
      "text": "Note: The risk of sovereign stress is a broader concept than debt sustainability. Unsustainable debt can only be\nresolved through exceptional measures (such as debt restructuring). In contrast, a sovereign can face stress\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00016",
      "start_char": 3060,
      "end_char": 3258,
      "text": "without its debt necessarily being unsustainable, and there can be various measures—that do not involve a debt\nrestructuring—to remedy such a situation, such as fiscal adjustment and new financing.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00017",
      "start_char": 3258,
      "end_char": 3491,
      "text": "1/ The near-term assessment is not applicable in cases where there is a disbursing IMF arrangement. In\nsurveillance-only cases or in cases with precautionary IMF arrangements, the near-term assessment is performed\nbut not published.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00018",
      "start_char": 3491,
      "end_char": 3716,
      "text": "2/ A debt sustainability assessment is optional for surveillance-only cases and mandatory in cases where there is\na Fund arrangement. The mechanical signal of the debt sustainability assessment is deleted before publication.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00019",
      "start_char": 3716,
      "end_char": 3943,
      "text": "In surveillance-only cases or cases with IMF arrangements with normal access, the qualifier indicating probability\nof sustainable debt (\"with high probability\" or \"but not with high probability\") is deleted before publication.\n"
